# The base image, pinned by content digest (D9).
#
# A tag is a moving target: `python:3.12-slim-bookworm` resolves to different
# bytes week to week, so an experiment that records only the tag cannot be
# rebuilt. The digest is what makes the environment fingerprint mean something.
#
# Re-pin deliberately, never automatically, and treat it as a dependency change:
#
#     docker pull python:3.12-slim-bookworm
#     docker image inspect -f '{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' python:3.12-slim-bookworm
#
# Paste the result below, replacing the whole line. Re-pinning changes the
# environment fingerprint of every subsequent experiment, which is correct —
# results from before and after are not interchangeable.
python:3.12-slim-bookworm@sha256:PIN-REQUIRED
